<section class="wrap dark" id="lab">
  <h2>Technical lab</h2>
  <p class="lead2">Small, runnable examples that show how I reason.</p>
  <div class="lab">
    <article><h3>Validate input at the boundary</h3>
<pre><code>from fastapi import FastAPI
from pydantic import BaseModel, Field

app = FastAPI()

class Query(BaseModel):
    question: str = Field(min_length=3, max_length=500)

@app.post("/ask")
def ask(q: Query):
    return {"received": q.question}</code></pre>
      <p><b>Why:</b> bad input is rejected with a clear 422 before it reaches the model or database. <b>Limit:</b> validates shape, not meaning.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Services in Docker Compose</h3>
<pre><code>services:
  api:
    build: .
    ports: ["8000:8000"]
    depends_on:
      db: { condition: service_healthy }
  db:
    image: postgres:16
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD-SHELL", "pg_isready -U postgres"]
      interval: 5s</code></pre>
      <p><b>Why:</b> the API starts only once the database is ready. <b>Limit:</b> add credentials via an env file, never in the repo.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Decision: when to use RAG</h3>
      <p><b>Choice:</b> retrieval over fine-tuning when answers must cite changing company documents.</p>
      <p><b>Trade-off:</b> retrieval quality now depends on chunking and indexing; answers need source links so users can verify them.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

