<section class="wrap" id="principles">
  <h2>Principles</h2>
  <ul class="principles">
    <li><b>Understand before building.</b> Define the problem first.</li>
    <li><b>Integrate, don't isolate.</b> Fit the tools people already use.</li>
    <li><b>Test assumptions early.</b> Cheap experiments beat late surprises.</li>
    <li><b>Design for real constraints.</b> Data, budget, latency, people.</li>
    <li><b>Document decisions.</b> Future maintainers need the why.</li>
    <li><b>Measure what matters.</b> Pick the metric before the feature.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="teaching" class="wrap">
  <p class="mono">Teaching</p>
  <h2>I teach what I deploy.</h2>
  <p class="lead2">I am a data instructor. Explaining a messy dataset to a room of learners trains the same muscle as explaining a system to a client's team: make it clear, show where it breaks, then fix it in front of them. Try a lesson below.</p>
  <div class="teach-facts" id="teach-facts" hidden></div>
  <div class="clinic" id="clinic" aria-label="Interactive data cleaning lesson">
    <div class="clinic-head">
      <span class="mono">Live lesson &middot; dirty data, step by step</span>
      <span class="mono" id="cl-count">5 rows</span>
    </div>
    <div class="clinic-body">
      <div class="cl-left">
        <div class="cl-table" id="cl-table"></div>
        <p class="cl-note" id="cl-note" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </div>
      <div class="cl-right">
        <h3>Revenue by city</h3>
        <div class="cl-chart" id="cl-chart"></div>
        <pre class="cl-code" id="cl-code" aria-label="pandas code"></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="clinic-ctrl">
      <button type="button" class="btn ghost small" id="cl-prev">Back</button>
      <div class="cl-dots" id="cl-dots" role="group" aria-label="Lesson steps"></div>
      <button type="button" class="btn small" id="cl-next">Apply next fix</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

